course: dictionary
lesson: 1618
title: What is a cheque?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cheque is a printed paper form. You write on it to tell your bank to pay money from your account to someone else. «A cheque is a written note telling your bank to pay someone; few people use cheques now.» The words "telling your bank to pay someone" are the clues that tell you what a cheque does.
explain: In money lessons you will see that a cheque is an older way of paying. You write the amount in figures and in words, then sign it. Many people now pay by card or phone, but grandparents still post cheques for birthdays.
explain: Some phrases use this word. You can write a cheque, pay by cheque, or cash a cheque. A blank cheque means permission to spend anything, so the clue is the word blank. In the US the word is spelled check, but it means the same thing.
fact: A cheque is a printed paper form used to pay money from your bank account.
fact: You write the amount in figures and in words, then sign the cheque.
fact: «Cheque» means a paper form that tells your bank to pay money; in the US it is spelled check.
fact: «Blank cheque» means permission to spend anything.
fact: Many people now use cards and phone payments, but grandparents still post cheques for birthdays.
exercise: «A cheque is a written note telling your bank to pay someone; few people use cheques now.» What is a cheque? | A bank building in town | *A written note telling your bank to pay someone | A coin you find in the street | A card you tap in a shop
exercise: Which phrase means permission to spend anything? | Pay by cheque | Cash a cheque | *A blank cheque | Write a letter
exercise: In the US the word is spelled check. What does it mean? | A money box | A type of cash | A bank card | *The same thing as a cheque
test: Which phrase means you give money to the bank by writing a paper form? | Blank paper | Pay by cheque | Cash a card | *Write a cheque
test: Why do some grandparents still post cheques? | *For birthday money | To tell the shop the price | To close their bank account | To pay for a bus ride
exam: Which of these is a newer way to pay than a cheque? | Writing a cheque in figures and words | *Paying by card or phone | Posting a cheque for a birthday | Signing a blank cheque
